{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WenzlBridgeApplicabilityQou","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WenzlBridgeApplicabilityQou","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_unique_in_qou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_unique_in_qou","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L122-L142","doc":"**Corollary.** Under the QOU substrate axioms, the Jones–Markov\n`y_λ` weights are uniquely determined and equal the Wenzl-bridge\nformula — no fitting parameter beyond `q` and the\n`tr_M(1) = 1` normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_applicability_qou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_applicability_qou","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L96-L117","doc":"**Step 4 (main applicability theorem).** Combining Steps 1–3,\nthe Markov trace on `H_n(R, q)` produced by the QOU fibre\nfunctor agrees with the Wenzl-bridge closed form\n`y_λ = s_{λ, r}(Q) / Σ_µ d_µ · s_{µ, r}(Q)` for `Q = q²`,\n`r` solved from `q · z = Q^r(1 - Q)/(1 - Q^r)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou","label":"prop:wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.unique","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The one-dimensionality of the Markov-trace family: any two trace\nfunctionals `tr₁ tr₂ : End_H(V^{⊗n}) → R` that share the Markov\nparameter `z` (via `appendGen`) and the normalisation `tr(1) = 1`\ncoincide on the whole carrier. This is the genuine uniqueness\ncontent (Chlouveraki HDR Thm 6.20), encoded as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim","kind":"class","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L75-L93","doc":"**Step 3.** Chlouveraki HDR Theorem 6.20 (= Juyumaya Thm 12,\n`d = 1`): the type-A Markov-trace family on `{H_n(R, q)}` is\none-dimensional in the trace functionals, parameterised by `z`.\n\n`tr_M(1) = 1` pins the scale; together with Step 2's `z`-value,\nthe Markov trace is unique. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.z_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.z_categorical","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.dimqV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.dimqV","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L71-L71","doc":"`z` is fixed by the categorical q-dimension constraint\n`z · dim_q V = 1`: there is a q-dimension scalar `dimqV` with\n`z * dimqV = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.markov_property","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.markov_property","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.appendGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.appendGen","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Markov property: appending a generator scales the trace by `z`.\nEncoded by a carrier endomorphism `appendGen` (right-multiplication\nby `σ_n`) with `tr (appendGen x) = z · tr x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L62-L62","doc":"`tr` is the restriction of the fibre-functor trace to the\nHecke-algebra carrier `End_H(V^{⊗n})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreFunctorMarkovTrace","kind":"class","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L51-L72","doc":"**Step 2.** The fibre-functor trace restricted to the\n`H_n(R, q)`-summand of `End_R(V^{⊗n})` satisfies the Markov\nproperty at parameter `z` fixed by the categorical q-dimension\nconstraint `z · dim_q V = 1`.\n\nFormal content: a `MarkovTrace` instance whose parameter `z`\nis computed from `dim_q V` via the categorical fibre functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.centraliser_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.centraliser_unit","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The centraliser **surjection** `H_n(R, q) ↠ End_H(V^{⊗n})` provides,\nin particular, a designated centraliser element (the image of `1`)\n— concrete witness that the carrier is inhabited.\n\nIt is a surjection, not an isomorphism, unless `N ≥ n` (`N = dim V`):\nbelow that its kernel is the span of the blocks with more than `N`\nrows.  This framework runs at `N = 2` with `n = 3A`, where the image\nis `TL_n(q)` of dimension `Catalan(n)` against `dim H_n = n!`.  The\ninhabitedness witness is unaffected — the image of `1` exists either\nway — so nothing below this line changes.\n\nSurjectivity is proved, for the presentation leg: `heckeToTL_surjective`\n(`QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb`, sorry-free) gives `H ↠ TL`.  The\nidentification `TL_n = End_H(V^{⊗n})` is stated, not proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.HeckeAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.HeckeAlg","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The Hecke-algebra carrier `H_n(R, q)`, whose image in `End_H(V^{⊗n})`\nis the centraliser.  Note the two are the *same* only when `N ≥ n`;\nsee `centraliser_unit` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.H","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L29-L29","doc":"The Tannaka–Krein Hopf algebra `H = Aut⊗(τ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.V","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L27-L27","doc":"The fundamental fibre `V := τ(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SchurWeylSetup","kind":"class","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean#L16-L48","doc":"**Step 1.** Schur–Weyl setup: under the QOU axioms (rigid braided\nmonoidal category C with self-dual fundamental object A, fibre\nfunctor τ : C → R-mod, Tannaka–Krein Hopf algebra\nH := Aut⊗(τ)), the Iwahori–Hecke algebra H_n(R, q) is the\ncentraliser of the diagonal H-action on V^{⊗n} where V := τ(A).\n\nStated as an axiom class; instances live in the QOU paper's\nstructural chapter.  This is the categorical input to the\napplicability chain. ","signatureChunk":0}]}